---- ALGORITHMS ----

>> A2: Explain your heuristic for deciding whether a page fault for an
>> invalid virtual address should cause the stack to be extended into
>> the page that faulted.

We define a heuristic valid_stack_access. There, it checks 
1) Fault address is in the user address space
2) The fault is close enough to the current stack pointer (32 bytes at most) because a legitimate access 
   like PUSH/PUSHA can access at most that much
3) The attempt is at most 8MB stack from physical base (a valid allocation within stack limit).

